9
00:00:31,660 --> 00:00:35,620
Before the directional drilling
begins, the directional drilling crew

10
00:00:35,620 --> 00:00:40,840
pre-plans the bore path to carefully
avoid obstructions such as other

11
00:00:40,840 --> 00:00:42,960
underground utilities.

12
00:00:47,900 --> 00:00:51,960
The horizontal bore begins with the
directional drill bit entering the

13
00:00:51,960 --> 00:00:53,240
entrance pit.

14
00:00:53,240 --> 00:00:57,320
The entrance pit is used to contain
and manage the drilling fluids.

15
00:00:57,540 --> 00:01:01,260
The directional drilling crew are in
radio communication with each other

16
00:01:01,260 --> 00:01:03,980
throughout the entire process.

17
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:06,900
The directional drill bit
is tracked by a sonde,

18
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:11,100
or radio detection device housed
within its extended connection to the

19
00:01:11,100 --> 00:01:12,860
directional drill pipe.

20
00:01:12,860 --> 00:01:16,280
The depth and pitch is sent to the
surface and received by the walkover

21
00:01:16,280 --> 00:01:17,760
locating device.

22
00:01:17,760 --> 00:01:22,440
The locator then gathers and interprets
the information and gives directions

23
00:01:22,440 --> 00:01:26,960
