which way to steer the drill bit.

24
00:01:27,160 --> 00:01:30,700
An experienced directional drilling crew
can navigate and steer the drill bit

25
00:01:30,700 --> 00:01:36,600
up, down, right, left and a combination
of varying degrees of each to drill a

26
00:01:36,600 --> 00:01:38,880
desired horizontal bore path.

27
00:01:38,880 --> 00:01:43,700
The drilling crew has the ability to
determine the exact depth and location of

28
00:01:43,700 --> 00:01:46,140
the drill bit at all times.

29
00:01:47,740 --> 00:01:52,380
A typical mid-sized directional drill
uses a 4-inch drill bit to drill a pilot

30
00:01:52,380 --> 00:01:53,360
